description.narrative:
This is a joint project for CARITAS KENYA and Catholic Justice & Peace Commission ( CJPC). The project seeks to empower community to demand accountability and establish strong partnership with local authorities (establish 4 county liaison offices) in ensuring quality service delivery. Project outcome areas include;
• Strong local and metropolitan structures within Catholic Church Structure • Enhanced civic/public and peace education • Community mechanisms on leadership and accountability. The project has a focus on a broad-spectrum and interlinked issues of governance, livelihood, climate change and disaster management &preparedness. It will establish community participation platforms/structures at the County level (citizen oversight forums) to engage stakeholders’ transparency and accountability in service delivery, take part in environmental conservation, disaster risk reduction, and civic education budget making processes at county level.
Church structures key to delivery of the project include; Bishop’s plenary assembly, adhoc bishop’s committees, Disaster Risk Reduction committees, liaison offices. CJPC commissioners, CJPC peace and development committees and CJPC and Caritas at Diocese and national level.
